<topic xml:id="autoyast-agama-compatibility-reference"
 role="reference" xml:lang="en"
 xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2"
 xmlns:its="http://www.w3.org/2005/11/its"
 xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"
 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
 xmlns:trans="http://docbook.org/ns/transclusion">
  <info>
    <title>Compatibility between &ay; and &agama; profiles</title>
    <!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
    <meta name="maintainer" content="souvik.sarkar@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
    <abstract>
      <!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
      <para>
        &ay; has long been the standard for unattended and automated installations in
        &productname; systems. &agama; takes a different approach to system configuration and
        deployment, using JSON or Jsonnet instead of the XML profiles of &ay;.
      </para>
      <para>
        This section lists, element by element, which &ay; profile sections carry over when
        migrating to an &agama; profile, based on the upstream compatibility matrix maintained by
        the &agama; project and cross-checked against the &agama; &ay;-conversion code as of
        2026-08-19, where noted.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <section xml:id="autoyast-compatibility-legend">
    <title>How to read the compatibility tables</title>
    <para>
      Most sections below include a table with the following columns.
    </para>
    <important>
      <title>What <quote>Supported</quote> means</title>
      <para>
        Each table lists only &ay; elements that &suse; officially supports in &agama;. An
        element that is not listed is not supported.
      </para>
    </important>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>&ay;</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Name of the &ay; element.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Supported</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Always <emphasis>Supported</emphasis>, kept as a column heading for consistency with
            the table's other columns.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>&agama;</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Name of the corresponding &agama; profile element, if any.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Notes</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Any comment or reason about the element.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </section>
