    <section xml:id="autoyast-scripts-chroot-scripts">
      <title><literal>scripts/chroot-scripts[]</literal></title>
      <para>
        This section is supported. The current &agama; converter (<literal>ScriptsReader</literal>
        in the &agama; source) maps <literal>chroot-scripts</literal> into the profile's
        <literal>scripts.post</literal> array, adding a <literal>chroot</literal> flag taken from
        the &ay; <literal>chrooted</literal> attribute. There is no separate
        <literal>scripts.chroot</literal> field in the &agama; profile schema.
      </para>
      <table frame="all">
        <title><literal>scripts/chroot-scripts[]</literal> compatibility</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <thead>
            <row><entry>&ay;</entry><entry>Supported</entry><entry>&agama;</entry><entry>Notes</entry></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row><entry><literal>filename</literal></entry><entry>Supported</entry><entry><literal>scripts.post[].name</literal></entry><entry/></row>
            <row><entry><literal>location</literal></entry><entry>Supported</entry><entry><literal>scripts.post[].url</literal></entry><entry/></row>
            <row><entry><literal>source</literal></entry><entry>Supported</entry><entry><literal>scripts.post[].content</literal></entry><entry/></row>
            <row><entry><literal>chrooted</literal></entry><entry>Supported</entry><entry><literal>scripts.post[].chroot</literal></entry><entry>Defaults to <literal>false</literal> if not set.</entry></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section xml:id="autoyast-scripts-post-scripts">
      <title><literal>scripts/post-scripts[]</literal></title>
      <para>
        This section is supported. Its scripts are merged into the &agama;
        <literal>scripts.init</literal> array together with <literal>init-scripts</literal>
        (below), with <literal>post-scripts</literal> entries applied first.
      </para>
      <table frame="all">
        <title><literal>scripts/post-scripts[]</literal> compatibility</title>
